# MIME types for media served from this directory.
#
# Apache's bundled mime.types (2.4.x on Windows/XAMPP) has no entry for .vtt,
# so caption files are sent with no Content-Type header. Browsers require
# "text/vtt" for a <track> element and silently ignore the captions otherwise -
# the file downloads fine (HTTP 200) but subtitles never appear, which makes it
# look like the caption files are broken when they are not.
#
# The video/audio types below are already correct in stock Apache; they are
# declared explicitly so playback does not depend on the server's defaults.
AddType text/vtt .vtt
AddType video/mp4 .mp4
AddType audio/mpeg .mp3
AddType application/pdf .pdf
